  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Linear antennas are considered to be those antennas that imply the use of electrically thin conductors having diameter much less than the wavelength of the electromagnetic wave passing through them.</p><p>The formula to calculate the effective power radiated by a linear antenna is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is a constant.</p></blockquote>",
